# Build output
*.exe
*.obj
*.o
*.a
*.lib
*.pdb
.vtmp/
vtext_build.*

# What an example writes when it runs. The pictures are output, not source, and committing one would
# make a change to the engine look like a change to the example.
examples/**/*.png

# Unicode Character Database: fetched by tools/fetch_ucd.v, not committed.
# The generated tables in ucd_*.v are committed, so a build never needs these.
# The small derived files are kept so the UCD comparison tests can run without a
# network fetch.
#
# The licence is kept with them, and that is not optional: UNICODE LICENSE V3 grants
# redistribution only on the condition that the notice travels with the files. A
# `ucd/*` ignore without a `!` for the licence publishes the data with no terms at
# all, which is the one thing that licence forbids. tools/fetch_ucd.v does not
# fetch it, so it is committed by hand.
ucd/*
!ucd/DerivedBidiClass.txt
!ucd/DerivedJoiningType.txt
!ucd/GraphemeBreakProperty.txt
!ucd/LineBreak.txt
!ucd/Scripts.txt
!ucd/PropertyValueAliases.txt
!ucd/ArabicShaping.txt
!ucd/LICENSE-UNICODE.txt
